                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1e85ffa-8418-30b8-a12f-f61892983f2a",
                                        "entry_id": "ce925696-a552-3cbc-a3e7-cf189b3f193e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The substance lining the bottom edge of an enclosure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fe894b8-76a0-4a9e-ba89-f7f49696004a",
                                                "sense_id": "c1e85ffa-8418-30b8-a12f-f61892983f2a",
                                                "text": "The substrate of an aquarium can affect the water's acidity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74d34ea6-1f4c-42f7-9820-507e6c151ae7",
                                                "sense_id": "c1e85ffa-8418-30b8-a12f-f61892983f2a",
                                                "text": "Stream substrate affects fish longevity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "281f871f-eb58-315f-afe8-95c93ae5082c",
                                        "entry_id": "ce925696-a552-3cbc-a3e7-cf189b3f193e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A substance acted upon, as by an enzyme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a09be47-62e0-339c-9bc3-85950e124fe5",
                                        "entry_id": "ce925696-a552-3cbc-a3e7-cf189b3f193e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surface on which an organism grows, or to which an organism or an item is attached."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2beb57f3-72ae-4ce1-a271-7bcdb0b719d5",
                                                "sense_id": "1a09be47-62e0-339c-9bc3-85950e124fe5",
                                                "text": "The rock surface of a rockpool is the substrate for a sessile organism such as a limpet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bc0b91b-1b2f-496c-a27b-b317d7c788ba",
                                                "sense_id": "1a09be47-62e0-339c-9bc3-85950e124fe5",
                                                "text": "This definition [of \"tool\"] is not simple, but contains several elements. The tool must not be part of the animal's body (a beak is not a tool); the user must manipulate the tool in some way for it to realise its function; and, finally, a tool cannot be attached to the substrate. This is a fairly clear definition, but does seem to produce some rather arbitrary distinctions (Hansell 1987b). The spider Dinopis, for example, makes a small web which it holds in its legs, thrusting it down on passing ants. This is a tool, but all other webs, however complex, are not since they are anchored to the substrate. The woodpecker finch […] that uses a fine stick held in the beak to extract insect prey from wood, is a tool user, but a shrike […] that impales an insect on a thorn still attached to the bush is not."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e10a292-9efd-40bd-be66-57437dafba66",
                                                "sense_id": "1a09be47-62e0-339c-9bc3-85950e124fe5",
                                                "text": "Detach/subtract [tasks involve] Severing a fixed attachment between environmental objects (or the substrate) or removing object(s) from another unattached object, so the latter is a more useful tool."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16a051b7-dc76-4c3f-901a-6f559885a43f",
                                                "sense_id": "1a09be47-62e0-339c-9bc3-85950e124fe5",
                                                "text": "Amphisteginids and peneroplids were among the few taxa found in the bay environments, probably due to their preferences for phytal substrates and tolerance to moderate levels of eutrophication."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24ca60c8-e3e5-3547-9e74-95be1a48f145",
                                        "entry_id": "ce925696-a552-3cbc-a3e7-cf189b3f193e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A language that is replaced in a population by another language and that influences the language imposed on its speakers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1757a244-2be8-39dd-bf66-2a3d3bc36257",
